## Key Concepts
- Consumer-driven contracts (PACT/OpenAPI) for API versioning
- Additive changes vs. breaking changes in REST APIs
- Per-tenant data isolation and security validation
- Latency SLAs and p95/percentile measurements
- Circuit breakers, retries, and fallback strategies
- Feature-flagged deprecations for safe rollouts

## Code Example
```javascript
// PACT consumer test for GET /orders/{id}
const { Pact } = require('@pact-foundation/pact');
const provider = new Pact({
  consumer: 'OrderUI',
  provider: 'OrderService',
  cors: true
});

describe('GET /orders/{id}', () => {
  before(() => provider.setup());

  it('returns order with optional shipEta', async () => {
    await provider.addInteraction({
      state: 'an order exists with shipping info',
      uponReceiving: 'a request for order details',
      withRequest: { method: 'GET', path: '/orders/123' },
      willRespondWith: {
        status: 200,
        body: {
          id: '123',
          customerNote: 'Please leave at door', // deprecated but present
          shipEta: '2024-12-25T10:00:00Z' // new optional field
        }
      }
    });

    const response = await axios.get(`${provider.mockService.baseUrl}/orders/123`);
    expect(response.data).to.have.property('shipEta');
    expect(response.data.customerNote).to.not.be.undefined; // backward compat
  });
});
```

